From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Vincent S. Cojot" <ElCoyote27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:47:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rpm: Add support for building akmod packages

Add akmod (Automatic Kernel Module) support to ZFS, providing a third
packaging option alongside the existing DKMS and kmod packages.

Akmod packages automatically build binary kmod RPMs when new kernels
are installed, enabling:
- Automatic kernel module rebuilds on kernel updates
- Distribution of binary kmod RPMs without recompilation
- Seamless minor version upgrades on RHEL/Fedora and clones

Key changes:
- rpm/generic/zfs-kmod.spec.in: Add conditional akmod support via
  rpmbuild --define '_enable_akmod 1'. When enabled, sets
  buildforkernels=akmod and repo=rpmfusion so kmodtool generates an
  akmod-zfs package. Add -common subpackage for shared license/doc
  files. Guard chmod and %files sections for empty kernel_versions.
  Make kmod-devel packages opt-in via %bcond_with devel to prevent
  akmods from installing unnecessary devel packages on every kernel
  update. When devel is not enabled, devel header files are cleaned
  from the buildroot to avoid unpackaged-files errors.
- config/rpm.am: Add 'make rpm-akmod' and 'make srpm-akmod' targets.
  These targets use the generic spec with _enable_akmod and
  intentionally omit kernel-specific defines (kernels, ksrc, kobj)
  so kmodtool enters its akmod-only code path.  The existing
  rpm-kmod/srpm-kmod targets pass --with devel to preserve the
  current behavior of producing devel packages.
- config/zfs-build.m4: Update comments to document the akmod vs
  regular kmod distinction for RPM_DEFINE_KMOD.
- scripts/kmodtool: Fix a pre-existing bug where
  print_rpmtemplate_kmoddevelpkg (the common kmod-NAME-devel package)
  was called inside the per-kernel loop in print_customrpmtemplate
  and print_rpmtemplate, causing duplicate %package definitions when
  multiple kernel-devel packages are installed. Move it outside the
  loop so it is emitted exactly once.

The akmod infrastructure requires the 'akmods' package to be installed
on the target system. When the akmod-zfs RPM is installed, it places
a zfs-kmod src.rpm in /usr/src/akmods/. The akmods service then
automatically rebuilds it for the running kernel via rpmbuild
--define 'kernels <uname-r>' --rebuild.

Usage:
  make rpm-akmod    # Build akmod-zfs, kmod-zfs (meta), zfs-kmod-common
  make rpm-kmod     # Build kmod with devel packages (unchanged behavior)

Tested on Fedora 43 (kernel 7.1), RHEL 9.8 (kernel 5.14), and
Alma Linux 10 (kernel 6.12). Verified akmods rebuilds produce only
kmod-zfs (no devel packages) after kernel updates.

Reviewed-by: Tony Hutter <hutter2@llnl.gov>
Reviewed-by: Brian Behlendorf <behlendorf1@llnl.gov>
Signed-off-by: Vincent S. Cojot <vcojot@redhat.com>
Closes #19099
(cherry picked from commit bb1c7ed97a92d77096852f063cbfdbfee177b185)
Signed-off-by: Stoiko Ivanov <s.ivanov@proxmox.com>
